==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|super|bug}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[strain]] of [[bacteria]] that is [[resistant]] to many [[antibiotic]]s ({{w|multiple drug resistance|e.g., MDR, XDR}}).
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Nicholas Kristof|title=The Spread of Superbugs|work=The New York Times|date=2010-03-07|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2010/03/07/opinion/07kristof.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=But now we’re seeing increasing numbers of '''superbugs''' that survive antibiotics. One of the best-known [is] MRSA, a kind of staph infection [that] kills about 18,000 Americans annually. That’s more than die of AIDS.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Any [[pathogen]] resistant to many, even all, of the biocides or other agents used to treat similar pathogens.
# {{lb|en|US}} An invasive [[insect]], {{taxlink|Bemisia tabaci|species}}, that is a major [[pest]] of vegetable crops, both directly and as a [[virus]] [[vector]].

